  "id": "Compound::DB00961 - Gene::6331",
  "verbalization": "Mepivacaine, a local anesthetic, is shown to bind to multiple sodium channel subunits—Scn8a, Scn4a, and Scn3a—each of which participates in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Scn5a, a key subunit of the cardiac sodium channel. The evidence suggests that Mepivacaine exerts its effects by modulating the function of voltage-gated sodium channels, which are critical for the propagation of electrical signals in cardiac tissue. The high scores from the three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Mepivacaine and Scn5a, supported by a shared pathway involving sodium channel activity. The mechanism appears to be mechanistically plausible, as the binding of Mepivacaine to multiple sodium channel subunits suggests a broad impact on ion channel function. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Mepivacaine may influence cardiac electrophysiology through its interaction with sodium channels, potentially contributing to its anesthetic effects.",
